      "title": "What this snapshot means",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "content": "### A reproducible view\n\nThe source rows are fictional and immutable. Controls change the view, not the saved evidence. Numeric ranges exclude missing or nonnumeric values; means remain unavailable when no numeric observations match.\n\n- [x] Use one dataset across widgets.\n- [x] Keep the selected parameters with an exported view.\n- [ ] Compare a second matched period."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "typescript",
          "title": "The same selection in JavaScript",
          "content": "const selected = rows.filter(row => row.station === \"North\");\nconst accepted = selected.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.observations, 0);"
        }
